### IntelliJ HTTP client examples. Start the server first.
GET http://localhost:8091/health

### Valid request
POST http://localhost:8091/echo
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "Ready to practise"}

### Validation error: expected HTTP 400
POST http://localhost:8091/echo
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": ""}

### Stage 1: whole IDs, memo commas and already-matched invoices
POST http://localhost:8091/reconciliations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage": "MEMO_ONLY",
  "payments": [
    "p1,500,Paying INV-12, thanks",
    "p2,500,Paying INV-1",
    "p3,700,Paying INV-12 again"
  ],
  "invoices": ["INV-1,500,2026-11-10", "INV-12,700,2026-11-12"]
}

### Stage 2: memo priority, then earliest due date and lexical ID for exact amounts
POST http://localhost:8091/reconciliations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage": "EXACT_AMOUNT",
  "payments": ["p1,1,INV-1", "p2,500,", "p3,500,"],
  "invoices": ["INV-1,500,2026-12-01", "INV-2,500,2026-11-01", "INV-10,500,2026-11-01"]
}

### Stage 3: exact amount wins first, then tolerance (inclusive) by due date
POST http://localhost:8091/reconciliations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tolerance": 5,
  "payments": ["p1,500,", "p2,500,", "p3,500,", "p4,500,"],
  "invoices": ["INV-1,500,2026-11-10", "INV-2,505,2026-11-01", "INV-3,495,2026-11-02"]
}

### Defaults: all stages, zero tolerance
POST http://localhost:8091/reconciliations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payments": ["p1,500,"],
  "invoices": ["INV-1,500,2026-11-10"]
}

### Row validation: HTTP 400 with invoice row number
POST http://localhost:8091/reconciliations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payments": ["p1,500,INV-1"],
  "invoices": ["INV-1,500,2026-02-30"]
}

### Invalid tolerance: HTTP 400
POST http://localhost:8091/reconciliations
Content-Type: application/json

{"payments": [], "invoices": [], "tolerance": -1}
